 "Memory climbs all seven scales as a single faculty. Scrub jays (JAH-ANII-000007) hold what-where-when records of thousands of caches — episodic-like memory in a bird. Humans add lifetime-crystallized knowledge (JAH-HUMI-000003) that keeps growing into old age, plus savant islands of extraordinary detail (JAH-HUMI-000021) revealing how much the brain stores beyond consciousness. AGI's continual learning without forgetting (JAH-AGII-000019) is the artificial counterpart: fast learning for the new, slow consolidation for the durable, rehearsal protecting what matters. Cultural accumulation (JAH-COLI-000015) externalizes memory across generations — no individual holds it all. The ladder tops at universal knowledge archiving (JAH-GODI-000013): the concept of memory at civilizational completeness. Each rung solves the previous rung's bottleneck: jays forget nothing they cached; humans forget but accumulate; AGI must not catastrophically forget; cultures archive; the God-mode concept loses nothing at all.",
